# ehthrow — LEGACY try/catch (the encoding PORFFOR emits). run(x): try { if x≠0 throw $e(x); else 7 }
# catch $e { payload+1 }. run(0)=7 (no throw); run(x≠0)=x+1 (payload bound + 1). Spec-sourced from
# the exception-handling proposal's legacy try/catch semantics; the official legacy/throw.wast (in
# eh_conformance_test) independently validates carder's legacy path. Raw unsigned bit patterns (D5).
invoke run i32:0 => return i32:7
invoke run i32:5 => return i32:6
invoke run i32:9 => return i32:10
